          "targetDoi": "10.1007/s00396-008-1882-2",
          "snippet": "The drop in the power coefficient at higher frequencies results from the shear based thinning of methylcellulose. Shear thinning is a well-known non-Newtonian property of fluids whose viscosity decreases under an increased shear strain  49  –  53  . Ghannam and Esmai  50  ,  51  have shown that the shear thinning depends on the concentration of carboxymethyl cellulose (CMC).",
